---
description: |
  Fetches the detection rules of the TruePattern TAXII collection as STIX 2.1
  Indicators.

  Every rule version is a separate Indicator: an update keeps the `id` and
  carries a later `modified` time. Use `truepattern::latest` to keep the
  current version of each rule.

  The operator fails on any warning during the walk, such as a malformed page,
  instead of emitting a partial collection.
args:
  named:
    - name: credential
      type: secret
      description: Base64 of the TruePattern `username:password` pair.
    - name: added_after
      type: time
      default: null
      description: Only fetches rule versions added to the collection after this time.
    - name: params
      default: {}
      description: |
        Additional query parameters. Pass `{"match[type]": "report"}` to fetch
        other object types instead of Indicators.
    - name: collection
      type: string
      default: "91a9eb95-e096-4774-80fb-6db78007a346"
      description: The collection ID.
    - name: base_url
      type: string
      default: "https://truepattern.io"
      description: The API base URL.
---

// Pages of 2,000 objects take about 14 MB, so a walk of all rule versions
// needs a handful of requests. Much larger pages risk a reset connection.
let $taxii_params = {
  limit: 2000,
  "match[type]": "indicator",
  ...({added_after: f"{$added_after}"} if $added_after != null),
  ...$params,
}
// Fail the walk on any warning, such as a malformed page, so that consumers
// never mistake a partial walk for the complete collection.
strict {
  stix::taxii::fetch f"{$base_url}/taxii/collections/{$collection}/objects/",
    headers={Authorization: f"Basic {$credential}"},
    params=$taxii_params
}
